diff --git a/apps/desktop/README.md b/apps/desktop/README.md
index 5f440e8..ac3e70e 100644
--- a/apps/desktop/README.md
+++ b/apps/desktop/README.md
@@ -30,10 +30,16 @@ The native market uses deepseek.stream's server search, categories, scenario tag
 
 The panel shows a persistent community sign-in entry and the signed-in account. Signing in resumes an installation the user has already confirmed. Community website pages open in the shared sandboxed Hub window with the current community sign-in session. Community login authorizes downloads; the official DeepSeek API key authorizes model adaptation. A paid plugin that requires website unlocking reports that requirement without repeatedly requesting login. Credentials stay in the main process.
 
+Desktop sign-in sends the canonical community Origin with the HTTPS account request. The panel distinguishes rejected account details, refused requests, rate limits, connection failures, invalid replies, and local storage failures without exposing server diagnostics. Community account changes atomically replace valid JSON configuration while retaining its other fields; failed sign-in and malformed configuration leave the existing file intact.
+
+The sign-in dialog's **Create a community account** and **Open Stream community** actions open `https://deepseek.stream/auth/register` and the community homepage in the system's default browser, retaining entered fields and any confirmed installation. After registering, return to Desktop and sign in to continue; browser registration does not automatically sign in Desktop. External account links carry no community session or login fields.
+
 Protocol links open confirmation in the same panel and never install before confirmation. The receiver accepts current website links, normalizes GitHub `owner/repository` selectors, and discards legacy account, permission, and target-profile fields. External HTTPS download origins appear in confirmation. An external website's protocol handoff confirms that Desktop was requested; the website does not receive installation progress from this receiver. Browser-side progress requires a paired website bridge.
 
 Compatible native ZIP/npm tgz bundles go directly to validation. Incompatible candidates can use the official `deepseek-flash` model with a locally configured official API key. The model receives bounded package source and sanitized diagnostics, and may patch only the extracted candidate while preserving package identity. Model attempts, time, context, and output have configurable limits. Downloaded archives and credential-free adaptation transcripts are retained separately from adapted artifacts. Desktop requests `raw=1` from the community download endpoint; an archive marked by the server as rewritten for Harness 0.1.6 requires model adaptation instead of being accepted as a current native bundle.
 
+First-party installations bind the selected plugin and release to the current community catalog. Package identity must match the recorded artifact's `sourceVersion`, falling back to `packageVersion`; its SHA-256, byte length, archive format, and `packageName` when present must also match exactly. Signed ticket URLs remain unchanged, and login and paid-unlock requirements remain enforced. Missing, stale, or failed metadata requires refreshing the market and retrying; Desktop never guesses a version or uses AI to bypass these checks.
+
 Only repository archives whose final download URL is canonical HTTPS `github.com/.../archive/...` or `codeload.github.com/.../(zip|tar.gz)/...` may omit tracked dependency and repository metadata directories such as `node_modules`, `.git`, and `.github` during extraction. Omitted entries still receive path, type, and duplicate validation and count toward entry and uncompressed-byte limits. npm archives and other origins retain strict extraction. Original archive bytes and their SHA-256 remain retained; retries using the same archive preserve its repository extraction rules.
 
 Adaptation requires the actual plugin implementation. AI cannot recover missing functionality from an archive containing only generated Harness 0.1.6 placeholder functions; its author must republish the real source. A download whose manifest version differs from the selected published version is rejected before paid model adaptation; the publisher must provide a matching archive.

diff --git a/apps/desktop/README.zh.md b/apps/desktop/README.zh.md
